      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The difference in flagging stems from the explicit nature of the language; Post 1 directly implies replacement or threat, which is a clear indicator of hate speech. Post 2's language is more coded nationalism, fitting a \"borderline\" category until more context confirms targeted attacks. For Post 3, the toxicity comes from the aggressive and dismissive confrontational tone, not just the slang, though \"fr fr\" contributes to the informal, aggressive nature.",
